Expo (React Native) app using expo-router. Screens live in `src/app/`, shared code in `src/`.
Start the dev server in a terminal with `{{#inDirectory "apps" appName}}{{runScript "dev:expo"}}{{/inDirectory}}`: it prints the QR code and takes the key commands (`a` Android, `i` iOS, `w` web, `r` reload).
`expo-dev-client` is a dependency, so the server starts in development-build mode: press `s` to switch to Expo Go, which needs no native build, or start with `{{#inDirectory "apps" appName}}{{packageRunner}} expo start --go{{/inDirectory}}`.
`{{#inDirectory "apps" appName}}{{runScript "android"}}{{/inDirectory}}`, `{{#inDirectory "apps" appName}}{{runScript "ios"}}{{/inDirectory}}` and `{{#inDirectory "apps" appName}}{{runScript "web"}}{{/inDirectory}}` start the server and open that platform.
{{#if (isMono)}}
The root `{{runScript "dev"}}` does not start this app: turbo's stream UI gives a task no terminal, so the server would print no QR code and take no key.
{{/if}}
{{#if (and (isMono) (eq pm "bun"))}}

`expo-doctor` reports `expo-constants`, `expo-font` and `expo-linking` as duplicate native modules in a bun turborepo. Expected: bun's isolated install links one version of each into this app and a second copy of the same version under `expo` and `expo-router`, and Metro bundles a single one. Do not add overrides or reinstall to silence it.
{{/if}}
